Read a replayed offer's age from the <call> wrapper, and filter RTP replays only on authenticated packets, with a cap.

Origin: fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector, on top of 0002 (upstream PR #26).

Why, defects in the PR #26 code on the inbound call path:

- PR #26 drops an offer replayed from the offline queue when its `e` attribute (the
  seconds the server held it) is over the caller's 90 s ring timeout, but reads `e`
  off the node CallOffer carries, and whatsmeow hands CallOffer only the <offer>
  child: `e` is on the <call> wrapper, so the check never fired and expired offers
  still rang. onCallRaw now reads the wrapper of a lone <offer> (the only shape
  whatsmeow dispatches as CallOffer) on the way in and marks the call;
  onOffer consumes the mark before any of its early returns and drops a marked one.
- rtpReplayFilter recorded (ssrc, seq) before SRTP authentication: a forged copy
  arriving through one relay suppressed the authentic one arriving through another,
  and packets claiming ever-changing SSRCs grew the filter without bound. The check
  (Seen) still runs first, the record (Record) now runs only once the packet
  authenticated, and at most 64 streams are tracked.

Found in the review of fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector#387, rounds 5, 6 and 11.

